menu "RGB status LED (drivers/rgb_led)"

    config RGB_LED_LEDC_TIMER
        int "LEDC timer"
        default 3
        range 0 3
        help
            Owned exclusively by this driver (DR10). Timer 3 leaves 0..2 for
            anything else that uses LEDC.

    config RGB_LED_LEDC_CHANNEL_BASE
        int "First of three consecutive LEDC channels (R, G, B)"
        default 5
        range 0 5
        help
            Channels BASE, BASE+1 and BASE+2 are owned exclusively (DR10). The
            S3 has eight low-speed channels; 5..7 is the top of the range.

    config RGB_LED_PWM_HZ
        int "Default PWM frequency (Hz)"
        default 5000
        range 100 40000
        help
            Above flicker perception and below the range where the duty
            resolution suffers.

    config RGB_LED_DUTY_BITS
        int "Duty resolution (bits)"
        default 10
        range 8 13
        help
            10 bits at 5 kHz needs a 5.12 MHz counter clock, which every LEDC
            clock source on the S3 provides.

    config RGB_LED_GAMMA
        bool "Square-law (perceptual) brightness curve"
        default y
        help
            Map an 8-bit level v to v^2/255 of full duty, so equal steps in
            level look like roughly equal steps in brightness.

    config RGB_LED_GAIN_R
        int "Default red gain (per mille of full duty)"
        default 1000
        range 1 1000

    config RGB_LED_GAIN_G
        int "Default green gain (per mille of full duty)"
        default 1000
        range 1 1000

    config RGB_LED_GAIN_B
        int "Default blue gain (per mille of full duty)"
        default 1000
        range 1 1000
        help
            The per-channel gains are the board's colour balance. A config's
            gain_permille overrides them; boards normally set these.

endmenu
